## Topics Revised

### 1. CSS Syntax
CSS uses selectors and declaration blocks to style HTML elements.

### 2. Inline vs Block Elements
- Inline elements take only the space they need.
- Block elements usually take the full available width and start on a new line.

### 3. Box Model
Every HTML element is treated as a box consisting of:
- Content
- Padding
- Border
- Margin

### 4. Div and Classes
- `div` is a container used to group HTML elements.
- Classes help apply the same CSS styles to multiple elements.

### 5. Margin and Padding
- Margin creates space outside an element.
- Padding creates space inside an element.

### 6. Borders
Borders create a visible boundary around an element.

### 7. Centering Elements
CSS provides different ways to center elements, including Flexbox.

### 8. Flexbox
Flexbox helps arrange and align elements inside a container.

Important properties revised:
- `display: flex`
- `justify-content`
- `align-items`
- `flex-direction`
- `gap`

